        "procedure": "Under a dry oxygen-free dinitrogen atmosphere using Schlenk techniques, triethylamine (10 mL of 0.1 M MeCN solution) was added to a solution of H2L (0.265 g, 0.50 mmol) and EuCl3·6H2O (0.365 g, 1 mmol) in 50 mL of MeOH. The mixture was stirred and refluxed for 30 min, cooled to room temperature, and filtered. Diethyl ether was allowed to diffuse slowly into this solution at room temperature, and pale yellow single crystals were obtained in one month.",
