        "property_type": "optical",
        "summary": "In CH3CN, CH3OH, and CD3OD, 1 shows typical Eu3+ 5D0 → 7Fj (j = 0–4) emission upon ligand-centered excitation with no ligand 1π–π* emission. Fluorescence quantum yields Φem are 0.093 (CH3CN), 0.040 (CH3OH), and 0.065 (CD3OD); yields are higher in CH3CN and CD3OD than in CH3OH, attributed to solvent exchange of coordinated MeOH. Ligand-centered absorptions of H2L are red-shifted upon coordination.",
